MetaWrap2 v=2.1.2
	Functional annotation subsystem: gene calling over bins or an assembly, KEGG orthologs at curated
		thresholds, module completeness, functional hierarchy and Krona wheels, AMR with context and an
		evidence level, viruses, strains, community appraisal, long reads and comparative genomics.
	New - `metawrap2 annotate`, replacing the Prokka wrapper `annotate_bins`: Pyrodigal gene calls over a
		bin folder or a whole assembly, one table every later step reads. Bins under 20 kb fall back to
		meta mode with a notice. Each gene carries `partial` and `distance_to_contig_end`.
	New - `annotate --kofam`: KO assignment at KOfam's per-profile cutoffs, compared on the score type each
		profile names (17,890 `full`, 8,697 `domain`). The 1,866 of 28,453 thresholdless profiles are dropped
		by default; `--kofam-relative-fraction` adds a fallback tagged evidence=relative (0.5x: +355 to 949).
	New - `annotate --kofam` accepts KOfam's per-KO profile directory (27,930 files) and searches it in one
		batch: 2,339 genes in 80 seconds at >1000% CPU (was one single-core search per file, >10 min).
	New - `annotate --pfam`: Pfam-A domains at each family's gathering threshold, per domain, with
		`pfam_architectures.tsv` and versioned accessions. One bin: KEGG places 1,620 of 3,891 genes (41.6%),
		Pfam 3,185 (81.9%), 1,578 with no KO; only 13 have a KO and no Pfam domain. InterProScan not wrapped.
	New - `annotate --cazy`: dbCAN in `--mode protein` on `annotate`'s proteins, with method agreement per
		row (two CAMI2 bins: 415 CAZyme genes, 274 backed by >=2 methods). CBM is kept apart from the
		catalytic classes. `metawrap2 install-db dbcan` fetches the pinned 7.4 GB release via `--aws_s3`.
	New - `metawrap2 pathways`: KEGG module completeness, both `pathwise` and `stepwise`. A `+`-joined
		complex counts as one step (31 of 573 modules are a single complex). Per-row flags: step count (47
		single-step), signature module, reactions with no KO (14), KO promiscuity, definition snapshot.
	New - functional hierarchy (BRITE ko00001: 8 branches, 57 processes, 570 pathways, 28,545 genes) per
		genome and per sample (abundance-weighted), with Krona wheels. A KO's weight is split across its
		pathways. The two non-biological branches are flagged; full and pathway-only wheels are written.
	New - `pathways -C depth.txt` (contig depth) and `pathways -G gene_abundance.tsv` (from `catalogue
		--quantify`) weight the sample hierarchy without MAGs. Gene-weighted profile: 33% "Not Included in
		Pathway or Brite" vs ~14% MAG-weighted. Every hierarchy row has a `weighting` column; one file each.
	New - `metawrap2 amr`: AMRFinderPlus on nucleotides over bins or an assembly, before any length filter.
		Each row has distance to contig end, a three-state context (`context_unknown` when not searched) and
		a Cao et al. 2026 evidence level (L1/L2 only). Virulence in its own table; co-located genes clustered.
	New - `amr --mobile-elements DIR` reads a `viruses` or geNomad output for MGE context. One CAMI2
		assembly, 18 calls: 5 on a plasmid contig, 1 with nothing within 10 kb, 12 undetermined. Dev bins:
		all four calls move from `context_unknown`/L1 to `no_mge_in_window`/L2.
	New - `amr --rgi`: RGI against CARD in its own env (`metawrap2 install-db card`, 4 MB). Joined with
		AMRFinderPlus on ARO accessions: five CAMI2 bins give 4 and 8 calls, 2 in common. RGI's tier
		(Perfect/Strict, Nudged suffix) is in `method`; `amr.tsv` gains an `aro` column.
	New - `amr` writes `amr_hamronized.tsv` (hAMRonization, 36 fields, tool and database versions read
		inside the env; `--skip-hamronize` turns it off) and `amr_normalised.tsv` (argNorm: ARO and drugs).
		argNorm gets only the AMRFinderPlus rows. Unmapped calls are kept and counted.
	New - `metawrap2 viruses`: geNomad and CheckV, the viral counterpart of binning plus refinement. One
		CAMI2 assembly: 0 viral contigs in the bins, 161 >=2 kb in the assembly (4 MIUViG high-quality), 344
		plasmids. CheckV's tiers; 16 unscored contigs are `undetermined`; 51 are lower bounds, so flagged.
	New - `viruses` clusters vOTUs at 95% ANI over 85% of the shorter sequence, longest member as
		representative (`--skip-votus` to skip). 161 contigs gave 161 vOTUs; a duplicate control collapsed.
	New - `viruses --crispr-hosts BIN_FOLDER`: CCTyper spacers matched exactly against viral contigs, trusted
		arrays only (`--untrusted-arrays` to include the rest). Dev set: 54 spacers, 0 matches to 161 viral
		contigs; the positive control finds all 54 in their own genomes.
	New - `metawrap2 appraise` (SingleM; `metawrap2 install-db singlem`): community share in the bins.
		ERR011347's 26 bins: 11.6% of bacteria, 25% of archaea; 323 lineages have no genome. Needs forward
		reads only, >=60 bp (34 bp trimmed reads gave 10 marker sequences, raw 75 bp reads 1,431).
	New - `metawrap2 nonpareil`: read-based coverage per sample and a cohort verdict. Three gut samples:
		84.4%, 74.6%, 89.4% coverage; Nd 17.97, 18.58, 17.27; 4.1x, 8.0x, 2.5x more sequencing to reach 95%.
		Model fit ported to Python, matches the R package to six significant figures.
	New - `nonpareil --kernel auto` picks one kernel per cohort: k-mer, or alignment if any sample's mean
		read length is under 2k. The kernels disagree (50.5% vs 83.0% on one sample). Reads shorter than k are
		filtered and reported; the alignment kernel is seeded `-r 1337`, the k-mer kernel cannot be.
	New - `metawrap2 strains` (inStrain): popANI, diversity gated on `breadth_minCov`, `--bam` for existing
		alignments. ERR011347-9 vs 26 bins: 42 comparisons, 17 at popANI >=99.999%, 4 over enough genome
		(60-92%) to count as shared strains.
	New - `strains --backend {instrain,tracs,both}`: TRACS transmission distances beside inStrain, never
		averaged. Both call bin.1 and bin.4 shared between ERR011347 and ERR011348. TRACS needs 25% breadth.
	New - `metawrap2 catalogue`: non-redundant gene catalogue across samples with MMseqs2 linclust (95%
		identity, 90% member coverage, `--cov-mode 1 --cluster-mode 2`). Gene ids are prefixed
		`<source>~<gene_id>`; `members.tsv` keeps the originals. No new install.
	New - `catalogue --quantify`: salmon (`--no-clip`) maps reads to the catalogue, writes gene abundance
		and a per-sample mapping rate, warns below 50%. Controls: own reads 100.0%, unrelated reads 0.68%.
	New - `metawrap2 quantify_function`: per-genome features weighted by genome abundance into sample tables
		in three units; the cross-sample unit needs `--microbial-fraction`. Module presence is binary above a
		threshold. `--abundance-kind` says whether to divide by genome size. Rows carry genome counts.
	New - `metawrap2 diff_abundance`: ANCOM-BC (scikit-bio 0.7.1), `feature ~ group` only. Refuses fewer
		than three samples or one group. Prevalence filter off by default; all settings recorded.
	New - `--biom` writes BIOM 2.1 (HDF5) tables, with the unit stored as sample metadata.
	New - long reads: `assembly -L reads.fastq --read-type ont-hq` (metaFlye) and `binning --long-read-type`
		(minimap2 preset, SemiBin2 long-read mode). `long_read_report.tsv` checks the declared platform.
		Simulated 25x R10 reads: 72 contigs, 2.41 Mbp, N50 57.9 kb, 4 bins.
	New - `metawrap2 pangenome` (PPanGGOLiN over dereplication clusters) and `metawrap2 phylogeny` (IQ-TREE
		on GTDB-Tk or `pangenome --msa` alignments, occupancy beside support). Cohort: 46 clusters gave 7
		pangenomes; <15 genomes is `partitioning_reliable=no`; <50% persistent is flagged.
	New - `binning --binsplit SEP`: multi-split binning of a prefixed catalogue, split per sample into
		`<binner>_bins_split/` and flat `<binner>_split_bins/`. Not a default: 29 clean HQ MAGs vs the cohort
		path's 34, 9.09 vs 8.71 cpu-hours, GUNC pass 70.2% vs 87.0%. Söding's +19%/+79% did not reproduce.
	New - bin_refinement reports the binned fraction in base pairs (CAMI2: 17.8% of contigs, 58.7% of bp)
		and a chimerism caveat (54.5-81.8% of HQ MAGs are single-strain; Treichel et al. 2026).
	New - measured module completeness vs MAG completeness (one CAMI2 genome): complete modules at 100/95/
		90/80/70/50% = 58/52.7/48.0/37.0/24.0/15.0. At 70/10, 59% are gone. `pathways` rows carry CheckM2
		completeness. Draws at 80% gave 31, 39 and 41. Details: bench_work/degradation/FINDINGS.md.
	New - vendored, dated KEGG snapshots: modules_table.tsv (573 modules; live KEGG has 582), ko_list.gz
		(28,453 profiles), ko_hierarchy.tsv.gz (64,956 KO-pathway pairs). KOfam HMMs are not vendored (KOFAM_DB).
	New - `benchmarks/make_release_figures.py` draws eleven release-note figures from module runs and skips
		any whose input is missing.
	New - docs: `## Function` and `## Viruses` in docs/modules.md, a worked chain in docs/usage.md
		(annotate -> pathways -> quantify_function -> amr -> diff_abundance). README updated to the current modules.
	Changed - CoverM in quant_bins filters reads at 90% identity and 75% aligned (were CoverM's 0 and 0).
		No flag restores 0/0.
	Changed - pins: `gunc >=1.1.1` (was >=1.0.6), `checkm2 >=1.1.0` (was >=1.0.2; also fixes the
		`_pywrap_checkpoint_reader` SystemError), `gtdbtk <2.5.0` (2.7.x wants R232 and ~140 GB RAM).
	Changed - `install-env --all` now also builds checkm2, gtdbtk, benchmark-amber and learned. It skipped
		them before, including SemiBin2, which the default binning tier needs.
	Changed - 2.0.x per-tool env names (nine) resolve to the 2.1 workflow env with a notice. Unknown names are
		refused with a did-you-mean. install-env, doctor and check share one resolver: 38 names over 11 envs.
	Changed - the MEGABLAST + taxator-tk path in `classify_bins` is deprecated (no upstream release since
		2015) and warns once. Default unchanged. `--gtdbtk` needs ~110 GB of GTDB data; nt needs hundreds of GB.
	Changed - `annotate_bins` is deprecated in favour of `annotate`; it still works.
	Changed - QUALITY_TIERS comments: `bins_medium_quality` (>=50/<10) is MIMAG medium, `bins_near_complete`
		(>=90/<5) is MIMAG HQ without rRNA/tRNA, `bins_high_quality` (>=70/<10) is not a MIMAG tier.
		Field names unchanged.
	Fixed - install-env on 2.0.1 could not reach bakta, checkm2 or gtdbtk under any name (KeyError, "No env
		file"). doctor invented env names and check printed "Preflight OK" after checking nothing.
	Fixed - `check` looked for tools on PATH; it now looks inside the module's conda env (PATH only with
		`use_conda_envs = false`). A tool missing from an existing env is reported as half-built (`--force`).
	Fixed - four help strings named envs removed in 2.1.0 (`metawrap2-annotate_bins-bakta`,
		`metawrap2-classify_bins-gtdbtk` twice, `metawrap2-bin_refinement-dastool`); a test now scans for these.
	Fixed - GUNC's pass column written as `1.0`/`0.0` was read as failing, in bin_refinement and the
		scorer: one 166-bin set scored 0 pass, wrong by 92 bins. `nan` is now unassessed, not failed;
		`gunc_unassessed_fraction` is reported.
	Fixed - `benchmark run --max-samples` kept one mate of each paired sample, and deinterleaved all ten CAMI2
		samples first (190 GB written for 57 GB used). Interleaved sample labels are left alone.
	Fixed - cctyper 1.9.0 from bioconda could not find its database (MetaWrap2 passes `--db`) and crashed
		on pandas 3 (envs/viruses.yaml pins `pandas <3`).
	Fixed - `install-env --from-lock` never used the lockfiles: the option was parsed and ignored, so every
		"reproducible" install solved the yaml. It now installs `envs/locks/<env>.<platform>.lock`, and says
		so when an environment has no lockfile for the platform and falls back to solving.
	Fixed - `install-env --lock binning` wrote `binning.linux-64.lock`; lockfiles are now named after the
		environment (`bins.linux-64.lock`), which is the name `--from-lock` reads.
	Fixed - `metawrap2 --dry-run install-env` built the environments instead of printing the commands.
	Fixed - pyrodigal and pyhmmer were imported but not declared, so `annotate` failed after a plain `pip
		install`. Both are now dependencies (pyproject and the conda recipe); a test checks that every
		module-level import is declared in both.
	Fixed - the top-level help ran `quantify_function` into its description; the column now fits the
		longest name. The `binning` entry lists all six binners.
	Changed - Python 3.14 is supported and tested in CI (3.10 to 3.14).
	Changed - the test suite is cut from about 1,360 tests to about 180: the golden tests, one main-path test
		per module, and the regression tests for defects that produced wrong output or lost runs. CI's
		CLI smoke test now reads the module list from the CLI, so new modules are covered.
	Changed - KOfam's thresholds and the BRITE hierarchy are downloaded at install time rather than shipped:
		`install-db kofam` (profiles plus ko_list) and `install-db kegg` (BRITE ko00001, config key
		KEGG_BRITE). Rows record the threshold list's md5 and the hierarchy's download date; `annotate`
		warns on a threshold list other than the validated one. `pathways` without KEGG_BRITE writes
		module completeness only.
	Changed - the Lockfiles workflow re-solves every environment monthly, one runner per environment, and
		pushes changed lockfiles to `chore/refresh-lockfiles`. It fails only on a broken solve or install,
		no longer when the repository does not let Actions open pull requests.
	Known issue - amr, viruses, strains, comparative, singlem, rgi, tracs and benchmark-amber have no
		lockfile yet, so `--from-lock` solves them from the yaml. The next Lockfiles run generates them.
	Known issue - geNomad needs the numpy pin in envs/viruses.yaml. A numpy in ~/.local can still shadow it
		under a bare `mamba run`; MetaWrap2 sets PYTHONNOUSERSITE=1 for its own env-wrapped commands.
	Known issue - long-read assemblies are not polished with short reads or merged with short-read
		assemblies.
MetaWrap2 v=2.1.1
	The top binning tier is an ensemble again, measured end to end, and tier cost is read from the run.
	Changed - `--preset slow` runs metaBAT2 + SemiBin2 + COMEBin (was COMEBin alone): end to end 64 HQ /
		60 clean vs 61 / 57, for 120.7 vs 80.8 cpu-hours and 2.4 vs 1.7 GPU-hours. `--comebin` restores the
		old tier. On the gold assembly the two tie (177 vs 176 clean).
	Changed - metaBAT2 is the third member on cost: a MaxBin2 trio covers 182 genomes vs 181, but MaxBin2
		costs 24.5 cpu-hours vs ~1.5 and 37.7% of its bins pass GUNC.
	New - bench_work/preset_cost.py and preset_gpu_hours.py read cpu-hours and GPU-hours out of `mw2 run`
		logs. The `default` tier's GPU figure is now 0.6 (was 0.8). Re-run counts matched: 14/14, 20/19, 30/27.
	New - docs/plan_functional_annotation.md and docs/plan_other_modules.md (not implemented). Licence
		findings: CARD/RGI and geNomad are non-commercial; KOfam's HMM profiles carry no licence statement.
MetaWrap2 v=2.1.0
	Defaults chosen by measurement, the first defaults moved, learned binners, cohorts, GUNC chimerism checks
		and the benchmark harness.
	Changed - `run` bins with metaBAT2 + SemiBin2 (`--preset default`); was metaBAT2 + MaxBin2 + CONCOCT.
		End to end: 53 clean HQ MAGs vs metaWRAP 1's 48, 43.8 vs 52.5 cpu-hours. Needs metawrap2-learned
		(~1.5 GB pytorch). `--preset fast` gives metaBAT2 + MaxBin2; `--metabat2 --maxbin2 --concoct` the old set.
	New - `binning --preset {very-fast,fast,default,slow}`. End to end on per-sample assemblies:
		  tier              HQ   clean   cpu-h
		  very-fast         39     36     92.1
		  fast              45     41     97.1
		  metaWRAP 1.3.0    52     48    132.0
		  default           56     53    127.1
		  slow              61     57    164.1
		Gold assembly, clean MAGs: very-fast 35, fast 59, default 114, slow 176. In this release slow is
		COMEBin alone (see 2.1.1). Named binners override a preset.
	Changed - the depth-table identity floor is 90% (was jgi's 97%). CAMI2: 47 clean HQ MAGs vs 35, AMBER
		F1 0.6624 vs 0.6371. `binning --min-identity 97` / `coverage --min-identity 97` restore it.
	Changed - binning maps with minimap2 (was bwa): depth Pearson 0.9461, AMBER F1 0.4519 vs 0.4493, 1.368 vs
		7.774 cpu-hours. `--aligner bwa` restores it; `--aligner bwa-mem2` matches bwa at 23.6 GB RAM.
	Changed - read_qc trims with fastp (was Trim Galore): +0.03% reads, +0.83% bases, 5.8% fewer cpu-hours,
		29% less wall time. `--trimmer trim-galore` restores it (0.1 GB peak memory vs fastp's 1.3 GB).
	Changed - quant_bins defaults to sylph (was salmon): Spearman 0.868 vs 0.827, 0.19 vs 1.08 cpu-hours.
		salmon is better on magnitude (Pearson 0.959 vs 0.811); `--quantifier salmon` restores it.
	Changed - `quant_bins --min-ani` defaults to 99 (sylph's own default is 95, where absent genomes took 55%
		of a sample's abundance vs 25%). `--min-ani 95` restores sylph's value; below 95 warns.
	Changed - metaBAT2 is seeded at 1337 (was a random seed per run); CONCOCT's seed 1 is passed explicitly.
		Unseeded runs differed by up to 294 contigs.
	Changed - GUNC runs on the final bins by default and adds gunc_css/gunc_pass to .stats.tsv; bins are
		annotated, never dropped. `--skip-gunc` turns it off (6.7 GB database, `metawrap2 install-db gunc`).
	Changed - bin_refinement reuses scores for identical bins (32% of 1,230) and records bins outside 200 kb-
		20 Mb as 0/100 without scoring (251 skipped, 0 passing bins lost). `--score-everything` disables the
		size filter. It now reports what its size filter removed.
	Changed - one conda env per workflow: 22 environments became 9. GUNC, DAS Tool, CoverM, fairy and Bakta
		are no longer opt-in; SemiBin2, VAMB and COMEBin share metawrap2-learned. 2.0.x env names stop
		working (aliases return in 2.1.2).
	Changed - the contig depth table is computed by metawrap2.depth (was jgi_summarize_bam_contig_depths):
		Pearson 0.9992 on means over 210,632 CAMI2 contigs.
	Changed - binning deletes per-sample BAMs, indexes and the aligner index once binners have their depth
		tables (`--keep-bams` keeps them). No module writes a SAM to disk; pipes run with `set -o pipefail`.
	Changed - blobology maps with minimap2 (was bowtie2) and takes `--aligner` (bwa, bwa-mem2); bowtie2 is
		no longer offered there. BAMs are no longer named <sample>.bowtie2.bam. read_qc still uses bowtie2.
	Changed - CONCOCT's numerical libraries run one thread per worker: 23.8 vs 29.9 cpu-hours, same bins.
	Changed - the very-fast tier's cost is 4.80 cpu-hours under minimap2 (was 22.9, a bwa-era figure).
	Changed - every command's help shows its default and accepted range (e.g. "[0-100] [default: 70]").
	Changed - rankings use clean high-quality MAG count with cost beside it, not MAGs per cpu-hour.
	Changed - docs consolidated into docs/; installation/, Module_descriptions.md and Usage_tutorial.md
		removed; WORK_SUMMARY.md is now docs/benchmarks.md.
	Changed - `benchmark score --checkm2` scores bins with CheckM2.
	Changed - the test suite pins use_conda_envs per test.
	Changed - none for assembly: MEGAHIT stays default. metaSPAdes gave N50 12,874 vs 9,325 for 3.2x the
		cpu-hours (245 vs 77), 140 vs 15 GB peak memory, 197 vs 228 Mbp. `--metaspades` for contiguity.
	New - `binning --semibin2` (2.5.0), `--vamb` (5.0.4), `--comebin` (1.1.0), all seeded, installed by
		`metawrap2 install-env learned`. VAMB: `--minfasta` 200 kb, `-o ''`, `-m 250`. None can run on the
		tiny fixture.
	New - `binning --device {cpu,cuda,cuda:N,auto}` for the learned binners, default cpu; replaces
		`--semibin2-engine` and `--comebin-device`. GPU: VAMB 13.8x and SemiBin2 4.9x cheaper; COMEBin on CPU
		does not finish (~1,485 cpu-hours projected).
	New - `quant_bins --quantifier coverm` (genome mode, strobealign) and `--quantifier sylph`; units differ
		from salmon's. `--quantifier depth` reuses binning's depth table: 0.013 cpu-hours, Spearman 0.780.
	New - `bin_refinement --consolidator dastool` (DAS_Tool 1.1.7, needs `-a`, `--search_engine diamond`).
		Per-sample bins: 0.62 cpu-hours and 10 bins vs the metawrap consolidator's 4.52 and 13.
		`metawrap` stays the default.
	New - `metawrap2 cohort`: per-sample assembly, one coverage pass, per-sample binning, one dereplication.
		Adds coverage and dereplicate, drops reassemble_bins by default; `-j N` runs N samples per stage.
	New - `metawrap2 coverage`: cross-sample depth in N alignments, not N^2, via a prefixed contig catalogue
		(`-a LABEL=path`, `--separator`, default `~`). `binning --depth` bins from an existing table.
	New - `coverage --coverage fairy` (opt-in): 0.04 vs 2.26 cpu-hours but 27 vs 37 HQ MAGs and 76% vs 87%
		GUNC pass in B5; single-sample AMBER F1 0.212 vs 0.452.
	New - `metawrap2 dereplicate`: skani, `--ani 95`, `--min-aligned-fraction 10`, single linkage,
		representative is the best-scoring member. `--copy` copies instead of symlinking.
	New - `assembly --aligner` for hybrid-path remapping; default stays bwa. minimap2 is 8.8x cheaper but
		labels 4,113,486 reads unassembled vs bwa's 2,867,680.
	New - `reassemble_bins --max-coverage` thins each bin's reads to 50x (default); `--max-coverage 0` keeps all.
	New - `metawrap2 install-db checkm2`.
	New - `mw2`, the same CLI under a shorter name.
	New - `metawrap2 benchmark list|fetch|run|score` with datasets and comparisons in benchmarks/*.toml,
		committed results in benchmarks/results/, a ~370 kB fixture, AMBER, CheckM, GUNC and abundance scoring.
		`--score-failed` scores crashed variants; `--reassess` re-runs assessors.
	New - benchmark B5: cross-sample coverage gives 37 HQ MAGs vs 32 single-sample, for 1.9 more cpu-hours
		of 90. Co-assembly is level at three samples: 85.1 cpu-hours and 81.4% GUNC pass vs 90.9 and 87.0%.
	New - benchmarks/coverage_fidelity.py compares coverage estimators per contig. CoverM reads 2.001x bwa
		because jgi filters below 97% identity.
	Fixed - MaxBin2 binned on depths `--noIntraDepthVariance` invented. Every earlier multi-sample MaxBin2
		result is affected. CAMI2: precision 0.6485 -> 0.8016, F1 0.4228 -> 0.4598, 188 bins -> 129.
	Fixed - quant_bins salmon tables were wrong with more than one bin (cumulative medians, NaN rows). Also:
		subfolders crashed it, .gz bins were refused, the two quantifiers labelled bins differently, and
		sample column order varied.
	Fixed - with one input bin set, metawrap_70_10_bins held every bin (376 where 178 pass 70/10).
	Fixed - unbinned.fasta was treated as a genome by bin_refinement, annotate_bins, classify_bins and
		reassemble_bins.
	Fixed - bin_refinement `--force` reruns failed at the end and kept the previous run's sets; `--resume`
		deleted the final bins it was resuming from. reassemble_bins had the same rerun defects.
	Fixed - reassemble_bins read filters used the NM tag, not FLAG: secondary/supplementary records became
		reads and a missing NM scored as perfect. The hybrid assembly now selects unmapped reads by FLAG 0x4.
	Fixed - `run` dropped learned binners before refinement, and any `--preset` but fast failed at refinement.
		Refinement now gets repeated `--bins`.
	Fixed - a co-assembly with no read_qc step had no reads; raw reads are now concatenated.
	Fixed - zero-length or all-N records broke samtools, VAMB and DAS_Tool; they are left out of working copies.
	Fixed - the depth samtools pipe could deadlock on unread stderr; the disk monitor could abort the wrong step.
	Fixed - CheckM1 lost its data path when its env was rebuilt; calls now set CHECKM_DATA_PATH from CHECKM_DB.
	Fixed - CheckM1 died with EOFError on deep output paths (unix-socket limit); a short symlinked temp dir is
		used, budget 75 characters. SemiBin2 uses the same helper.
	Fixed - a missing opt-in env or missing mamba is reported before the run, not at the first tool.
	Fixed - doctor/install-env: opt-in envs went unreported, shared envs passed "0/0 tools OK", `--lock`
		failed, GUNC's .dmnd was reported missing, opt-in names raised KeyError, `--force` never rebuilt.
	Fixed - env-wrapped commands set PYTHONNOUSERSITE=1, so ~/.local packages no longer shadow env pins.
	Fixed - an aligner crash in binning or reassemble_bins read as success (no pipefail).
	Fixed - a background run ignored SIGINT; an interrupt could orphan a running tool.
	Fixed - `--semibin2`/`--vamb`/`--comebin` help named env names that no longer exist.
	Fixed - benchmark harness: read_qc counts were one mate's; refinement arms dropped bin sets past three;
		crashed variants were scored; clean HQ was HQ x GUNC pass (COMEBin 158 -> 176); re-scores summed;
		CAMI2 contig names and reads_glob were mishandled; AMBER scored one file twice. Plus smaller fixes.
	Removed - `binning --subsample` and `coverage --subsample`: half the reads kept 33 of 37 HQ MAGs to save
		~1% of a run.
	Known issue - the identity floor divides by query length (`qlen`), not aligned length, so it is looser
		than asked under soft-clipping. Agrees with jgi at Pearson 0.9992; unchanged.
	Known issue - CONCOCT under Python 3.12 costs several times its Python 2.7 + MKL build (5.6 cpu-hours).
	Known issue - DAS_Tool fails on the 159 Mb remainder "bin" from a pooled gold assembly.
MetaWrap2 v=2.0.1
	Pipeline driver, verified resume, run history, one bin naming convention, one-command install, and
		fixes from an end-to-end run on 3 metaHIT gut metagenomes. No scientific behaviour changed.
	New - `metawrap2 run <sheet|directory> -o study/` runs a study from a TOML/YAML sheet: `-j`,
		`--resume`, `--dry-run`, `--steps`/`--skip`, `--no-coassembly`. `metawrap2 run --example` prints a sheet.
	New - `metawrap2 quickstart` builds and verifies every env (`--binning-only`, `--from-lock`). Databases
		download only with `--databases small|full|none`.
	New - `metawrap2 install-db` downloads, indexes and configures databases (`--list`, `--small`).
		`install-env -t N` / `install-db -t N` work in parallel.
	New - `metawrap2 config migrate <file>` converts an old KEY=/path config to TOML without executing it.
	New - --resume verifies: a step is skipped only if completed, outputs present and non-empty, inputs
		unchanged (manifest.json). `--strict-fingerprints` hashes whole files.
	New - `metawrap2 status <study>` (`--step`, `--audit`, `--json`); the audit also runs after every run.
	New - `metawrap2 history` (~/.metawrap2/history.jsonl) with filters and `--diff RUN RUN`.
	New - committed conda lockfiles (`install-env --lock`, `--from-lock`, `doctor --fix --from-lock`).
	New - provenance: run_environment.json, git commit and dirty state, database fingerprints, per-step peak
		RSS/CPU/wall. `metawrap2 calibrate` compares disk and memory estimates with real runs.
	New - inputs are checked for empty, malformed, truncated and bad-gzip files before tools run.
	New - SIGTERM/SIGHUP handled like Ctrl-C (exit 128 + signal); one writer per output directory (lock,
		`--force` overrides); `-m` is divided across `-j` workers.
	New - scratch_dir / $METAWRAP2_SCRATCH sets one scratch location; run log rotates at 256 MB, 3 backups.
	New - paired reads recognised as _1/_2, _R1/_R2, _R1_001/_R2_001, .1/.2; .gz and .bz2 throughout.
		read_qc gains `--single-end` and `--interleaved`.
	New - bin_refinement takes up to six bin sets (`--refine-combinations pairs-and-all|pairs|all`); two-
		and three-set output is byte-identical.
	New - `metawrap2 doctor` (= `metawrap2 test`), `--fix` rebuilds broken envs; also checks databases.
	New - opt-in tools wired up: `bin_refinement --checkm2`, `classify_bins --gtdbtk`, `annotate_bins --bakta`.
	New - progress bars on long loops (stderr, terminal only); retired names like `kraken` and --metabat1
		say what replaced them.
	Changed - bins are named bin_001.fasta for every binner (were bin.1.fa, bin.0.fa or CONCOCT ids); use
		*.fasta and `-x fasta`. Contents unchanged.
	Changed - .stats is now .stats.tsv and .contigs is .contigs.tsv.
	Changed - Python 3.10 minimum (was 3.8).
	Changed - --resume re-runs a step it cannot verify, so a resume may now do work that used to be skipped.
	Changed - the disk-space preflight warns instead of refusing; `strict_space_check = true` restores the stop.
	Changed - unknown [settings] keys are errors with a did-you-mean; unknown [databases] keys are notes.
	Changed - `-t` defaults to [settings] threads (was 1) and accepts `-t all`; Trim Galore gets `-j` (<=4).
	Changed - logging writes <output>/metawrap2.log; repetitive tool output is collapsed (1.8 MB -> 30 KB on
		a 3-sample run), `--verbose-logs` for raw output.
	Changed - pip-installable wheel with envs as package data; 456 tests (was 245) gate pushes; ruff
		findings 564 -> 0; mypy in CI.
	Fixed - helper scripts ran inside module envs without Python and failed (bin_refinement,
		reassemble_bins, quant_bins, blobology).
	Fixed - mamba 2.x choked on `--no-capture-output`; `metawrap2 test` reported every tool MISSING.
	Fixed - env yamls: blobology could not be created, classify_bins lacked blast, assembly pins python<3.12,
		bin_refinement pins setuptools<81; numpy/pandas/matplotlib/seaborn/scipy/tqdm declared.
	Fixed - metaBAT2 2.18 header annotations broke contig matching: refinement never merged metaBAT2 bins
		and quant_bins aborted. Contig id is now the header up to the first whitespace.
	Fixed - read_qc with `--skip-trimming --skip-bmtagger` moved the user's raw FASTQ; decompressed copies
		were left behind.
	Fixed - CONCOCT clusters were split at the first "." in contig names, scattering metaSPAdes contigs.
	Fixed - metaBAT2's non-genome outputs were scored as bins; now moved to metabat2_extra/. Its bins are
		renumbered numerically.
	Fixed - `--dry-run` stopped after one or two commands; `run --dry-run` executed the run.
	Fixed - history recorded every run as "completed" whatever the outcome.
	Fixed - kraken2 `--subsample` held all reads in memory; now reservoir sampling.
	Fixed - kraken2 taxonomy in prebuilt layouts, "superkingdom" renamed "domain", TAXATORTK_TAXONOMY_NCBI
		for binner/taxknife, BLAST v5 3-digit volumes (BLASTDB_NAME), relative `-o` paths.
	Fixed - the driver passed fixed -A/-B/-C to bin_refinement, failing when some binners were not selected.
	Fixed - dereplication crashed on a bin with no stats row; rm_short_contigs relied on SPAdes headers;
		MEGAHIT names read by position; sam_to_fastq wrote ">" headers.
	Fixed - `metawrap2 check` exits non-zero on a missing required database.
	Fixed - smaller issues: single-sample salmon dirs kept, blobplot bins matched nothing, needless bin
		rewrites, failed SPAdes reassembly now shows its errors, annotate_bins read sidecar files.
	Known issue - install-env cannot reach bakta, checkm2 or gtdbtk under any name; create them with
		`mamba env create -f <envs>/<name>.yaml`. Fixed in 2.1.2.
MetaWrap2 v=2.0.0
	Python-native successor to metaWRAP: same algorithms, tools and results as metaWRAP 1.x, no Bash,
		Perl or R, modern packaging and per-module conda environments.
	New - command is `metawrap2`; modules unchanged; `python -m metawrap2.modules.<module>` also works.
	New - per-module conda env "metawrap2-<module>", driven with mamba; `use_conda_envs=false` uses PATH.
	New - module commands are editable templates; constants overridable in ~/.metawrap2/config.toml.
	New - `metawrap2 check`, `metawrap2 install-env`, `metawrap2 test` (reports tool versions),
		`metawrap2 config init|show`, `metawrap2 completion bash|zsh`. One handler runs every external command.
	New - provenance per run: run_config.json, run_commands.txt, provenance.txt, run.stdout/run.stderr.
	New - global `--dry-run`, `--force`, `--resume` (state in <outdir>/.metawrap2/steps).
	New - warnings for paths with spaces or shell metacharacters; CI on Python 3.8-3.12, mkdocs site.
	Changed - configuration moved from the sourced config-metawrap to metawrap2.toml.
	Changed - blobology and Binning_refiner steps run in Python; flowcharts built by
		flowcharts/make_flowcharts.py.
	Removed - kraken1 module (use kraken2) and metaBAT1 binner (use metaBAT2).
	Changed - from metaWRAP 1.x: replace "metaWRAP" with "metawrap2"; see README "Coming from metaWRAP 1.x".

metaWRAP v=1.5 (superseded by MetaWrap2 2.0.0)
	General
		Python scripts now run under Python 3 (Python 2 reached end of life)
		sequence inputs can now be gzip- or bzip2-compressed (.gz/.bz2)
		added "check" command to verify tools and databases are available before a run
		dependencies loosened from old fixed versions and grouped by module under envs/
		clearer, tool-specific error messages when an external program fails
		reset the example database paths in config-metawrap to generic placeholders
	Read_QC
		gzipped read files (.gz) are now accepted as input
	Bin_refinement
		use a portable method to measure bin file sizes (works on macOS/BSD)
		bin consolidation is now deterministic regardless of input ordering
	Blobology
		bowtie2-build now uses the requested number of threads
		replaced the Perl and R helper scripts with Python; the contig annotation
			table and blobplot images are now generated with Python (no Perl/R needed)
	Reassemble_bins
		reassembly now uses one thread per bin as documented, reducing oversubscription

